    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI found that `comment and multiply` is a very commonly used operation\n\nbased on this post:\n\nhttps://www.reddit.com/r/neovim/comments/1k4efz8/comment/mola3k0/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web3x&utm_name=web3xcss&utm_term=1&utm_content=share_button\n\nI come up with:\n\n```lua\noperatorfunc = function(_)\n\tlocal pos10_a = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_mark(0, \"[\")\n\tlocal pos10_b = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_mark(0, \"]\")\n\tlocal pos00_a = {\n\t\tpos10_a[1] - 1,\n\t\tpos10_a[2],\n\t}\n\tlocal pos00_b = {\n\t\tpos10_b[1] - 1,\n\t\tpos10_b[2],\n\t}\n\n\tlocal lines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, pos00_a[1], pos00_b[1] + 1, true)\n\n\trequire(\"mini.comment\").toggle_lines(pos10_a[1], pos10_b[1])\n\n\tvim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(\n\t\t0,\n\t\tpos00_b[1] + 1,\n\t\tpos00_b[1] + 1,\n\t\ttrue,\n\t\tlines\n\t)\n\n\tvim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, {pos10_b[1] + 1, 0})\n\tvim.cmd(\"normal! _\")\nend\n\nvim.keymap.set(\n\t{\"n\", \"x\"},\n\t\"yc\",\n\tfunction()\n\t\tvim.o.operatorfunc = [[v:lua.operatorfunc]]\n\t\treturn \"g@\"\n\tend,\n\t{\n\t\texpr = true,\n\t}\n)\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"ycc\", \"yc_\", {remap = true})\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"yC\", \"yc$\", {remap = true})\n```\n\nI think maybe this feature could be added to mini.comment",
