            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI do agree that \"multiply and comment\" is a common operation, but the problem here is that there is no good LHS keys to map to. I strongly believe that making a mapping that starts from *any* currently defined operator (like `y`, `d`, `c`, `gc`; `gm`, `gr`, etc. from 'mini.operators') leads to issues that will be unexpected and hard to figure out why they are happening. The reason is that making also affects Operator-pending mappings for text-objects. For example, making a `yc` operator will make it very hard in practice to have a textobject that starts with `c`: yanking such textobject will require a 'timeoutlen' milliseconds pause after `y` in order to avoid activating `yc` operator.\n\nThe only counter-argument here to be made is that there are already built-in `cc`, `dd`, `yy` \"actions\" and thus making textobjects that start with `c`, `d`, and `y` is already a bad idea. This might be valid, but I need time to think about it.\n\nMeanwhile I'll close this as \"unplanned (for now)\".\n\n---\n\nNote: also see #730 for some other approaches.",
